    {
      "id": "03-create",
      "instruction": "In this Odoo backend, create a new quotation (Sales app > Quotations > New) for the customer '{{runid}} Bench Customer' (choose the customer from the autocomplete dropdown - the value must be selected from the dropdown, not just typed). Add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again select it from the autocomplete dropdown so the unit price fills in automatically), and set the quantity to 3. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, (c) the untaxed amount the app computes for the quotation, and (d) the quotation's reference/name (e.g. S00042). Do not confirm the order - leave it as a draft quotation.",
      "outputs": [
        "customer",
        "product_name",
        "unit_price",
        "quantity",
        "line_subtotal",
        "untaxed_amount",
